                    insight_authentic:      `Authentic change leadership: you led against your instinct, not from it. Adoption is real, trust held above the floor, the anchor became an advocate, and your EI alignment shows you chose your authentic voice consciously rather than acting out your defaults.`,
                    insight_announce:       `You hit adoption but trust slipped. A change that runs on a high-trust culture can't be banked on launch energy alone — the announcement-vs-adoption gap and a wobbling promise will pull the numbers back unless trust is repaired.`,
                    insight_short:          `Adoption stalled below the board's bar. The division half-believed and half-feared, and without a self-aware, coaching-led approach the doubt won. Re-examine where instinct overrode discipline.`,
                    insight_broken:         `The 144-year promise broke: trust fell through the floor or reskilling was underfunded into redundancies. The firm's deepest cultural asset became its biggest liability — and that, not the plan, is what the division will remember.`,
                    insight_leak:           `A hidden truth or an over-promise detonated when the closure list leaked. In a trust culture, the leader who wasn't straight pays in collapsing trust — candour up front would have cost far less.`,
